f the virus causing the current outbreak. New research raises hopes of protection against the various types of Ebola.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Africa's ANC facing worst-ever performance in local elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:21638d9fb1dc2787ab5f4cb651188c41005208f4b136fb37d1411b08b9199f6b</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T18:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-africa-s-anc-facing-worst-ever-performance-in-local-elections/a-79887482--0f01de17e4d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-africa-s-anc-facing-worst-ever-performance-in-local-elections/a-79887482?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Near-final results show South Africa's once dominant ANC will see its lowest-ever vote percentage. The party is taking the blame for shoddy municipal services, including water and electricity shortages.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Zambia's opposition criticizes government restructuring and layoffs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:598b5cfe94c726892306ac39e4a2396281d2f0f6c2faffc99f2898df85c1161e</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T13:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/zambia-s-opposition-criticizes-government-restructuring-and-layoffs/a-79875892--f6feaaea394e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/zambia-s-opposition-criticizes-government-restructuring-and-layoffs/a-79875892?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Government-backed dismissals and restructuring are fueling debate in Zambia. Opposition politicians are questioning the transparency of the plans; officials say the changes are necessary.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Wawira Njiru, Kenya's school feeder and German Africa Prize recipient</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:38b244c1fe6603721cea95e20eab1058f07c888abb070023ed2435ccca160d98</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T10:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wawira-njiru-kenya-s-school-feeder-and-german-africa-prize-recipient/a-79646537--47b719bb31e0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wawira-njiru-kenya-s-school-feeder-and-german-africa-prize-recipient/a-79646537?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Standing ovations in Berlin: Kenyan social entrepreneur Wawira Njiru received the German Africa Award for her school feeding programme, which now provides meals to 730,000 children every day.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Will renewed conflict derail Ethiopia's economic growth?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a102b677a2e73eff4237197713f83d563ac813a66d55aafcdb1dbe82aa63160a</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T11:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-renewed-conflict-derail-ethiopia-s-economic-growth/a-79807060--aec9783cc542.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-renewed-conflict-derail-ethiopia-s-economic-growth/a-79807060?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ethiopia's economy is growing strongly. But renewed fighting in the north of the BRICS member state could deter investment, strain public finances and push up the cost of living.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
